VACUITY GUARD, recorded because the first run of MUT-Z2 exposed it. On
the first attempt only ONE of those four flipped: the other three are
`all(...)` quantifiers, which are vacuously TRUE over an empty list, so a
mutant that emptied `capability_evaluations[]` entirely satisfied them.
Each of the three now additionally requires
`len(published_evaluations) == len(registry_ids)`, and the re-run above
shows all four flipping. The vacuity was found by the mutation, not
argued away.

MUT-M3 (the suite's own standing RED mutant, union-match -> intersection-
match) also kills five of this fixture's assertions independently, for a
different reason worth naming: under the intersection reading `all([])`
is vacuously true, so EVERY Capability "matches" on zero affected
components -- precisely the inverted answer REQ-006(g) exists to forbid.
